  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe notation $3∣6$ means {{field-1}}. It is equivalent to the statement that there exists {{field-2}} $k$ such that {{field-3}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$ So, $3∣6$ means $3\\text{ divides }6.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $3∣6$ is equivalent to the statement that there exists $\\text{an integer}$ $k$ such that $6=3k.$",
